    "outcome_summary": "The publication presented the PISA for Development framework rather than empirical results, describing how PISA was adapted to better serve middle- and low-income countries. It outlined the expanded cognitive frameworks for reading, mathematics, and science, including lower proficiency levels and out-of-school assessment components, and explained the contextual questionnaire framework built around educational prosperity, equity, and poverty-related measures. The report also documented the participating countries, implementation phases, and capacity-building strategy for the pilot project. No statistical modeling or predictive analysis was reported.",
